cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EISForge in your research, please cite it using this metadata."

title: "EISForge: Physics-Informed Machine Learning for Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy"
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-06-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hj1308/EISforge-"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20649692
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20649692"

authors:
  - family-names: Jafari
    given-names: Hoda
    email: hoda.jaafari@gmail.com
    orcid: ""

abstract: >
  EISForge is an open-source Python framework for Electrochemical Impedance
  Spectroscopy (EIS) analysis. It combines classical CNLS fitting with
  Kramers-Kronig validation, CV/LSV analysis, ECSA calculation, a
  literature-guided knowledge base (195 peer-reviewed papers), and a
  Physics-Informed Transformer architecture (EIS-GPT). Supports Autolab (.idf),
  Gamry (.dta), and generic CSV file formats.

keywords:
  - electrochemical impedance spectroscopy
  - EIS
  - CNLS fitting
  - equivalent circuit
  - cyclic voltammetry
  - machine learning
  - electrochemistry
  - alcohol oxidation reaction
  - Kramers-Kronig
  - open source

